The audience is first-time, never-licensed Vermont applicants, typically teenagers on the learner's permit and junior license path and adults applying for a first driver's license, reading at a plain-English level with no assumed driving vocabulary. This section teaches when and how a vehicle must be registered and plated, the bill of sale and title steps for a sale or trade, the purchase and use tax rate, title exceptions, vehicle identification numbers and rebuilt titles, liens, the required liability insurance amounts and the penalties for lacking proof, the yearly inspection, and the handbook's efficient driving tips. The content assumes no prior rule knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy; every term the section introduces is defined in the glossary lines of part C.
